cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'HL7 for Rust: parse, navigate, validate, modify, and render HL7 messages'
message: >-
  If you use this work and you want to cite it,
  then you can use the metadata from this file.
type: software
# The workspace's 14 crates version independently (see CHANGELOG.md); the
# version cited here is the umbrella `hl7` crate's, which re-exports the
# rest, and the date is that release's date.
version: 0.1.5
date-released: '2026-08-26'
authors:
  - given-names: Joel Parker
    family-names: Henderson
    email: joel@joelparkerhenderson.com
    affiliation: joelparkerhenderson.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4681-282X'
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: 'https://github.com/hl7-rust/hl7-rust/'
    description: 'HL7 for Rust: the Cargo workspace holding every crate in the project'
  - type: url
    value: 'https://hl7-rust.github.io'
    description: 'HL7 for Rust: documentation, guides, tutorials, and examples'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/hl7-rust/hl7-rust/'
url: 'https://hl7-rust.github.io'
abstract: >-
  A Cargo workspace of Rust crates that parse, navigate, validate, modify,
  and render Health Level Seven (HL7) messages. One crate per layer, one
  module per standard: HL7 v2 releases 2.1 through 2.9 in the ER7
  pipe-delimited encoding, transports for MLLP over TCP and SOAP over HTTP,
  conversions between ER7 and both v2.xml and JSON, and an HL7 v3
  foundation of RIM backbone classes and the three-level message envelope.
keywords:
  - hl7
  - hl7-v2
  - er7
  - healthcare
  - health-informatics
  - interoperability
  - mllp
  - rust
